{"name":"Placebo","hex":"#e7e7e7","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"placebo","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A dummy medicine containing no active ingredients; an inert treatment. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","The vespers sung in the office for the dead."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/placebo"}],"entries":[{"title":"Placebo","blocks":[{"text":"A placebo is a medicine or treatment intended to appear genuine to its recipient, but which has no pharmaceutical effect. Common placebos include inert tablets, inert injections, sham surgery, and other procedures."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Cebocap.jpg/330px-Cebocap.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Placebo","wikidata":"Q269829"},{"title":"Placebo (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Placebo are a British alternative rock band, formed in London in 1994 by vocalist-guitarist Brian Molko and bassist-guitarist Stefan Olsdal, who have remained the two constant members, with three full-time drummers throughout the band's existence."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Placebo_-_2022155210134_2022-06-04_Rock_am_Ring_-_Sven_-_1D_X_MK_II_-_1915_-_B70I0956.jpg/330px-Placebo_-_2022155210134_2022-06-04_Rock_am_Ring_-_Sven_-_1D_X_MK_II_-_1915_-_B70I0956.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Placebo_(band)","wikidata":"Q484839"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/%22Miracle_Cure%21%22_Health_Fraud_Scams_%288528312890%29.jpg/500px-%22Miracle_Cure%21%22_Health_Fraud_Scams_%288528312890%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/%22Miracle_Cure%21%22_Health_Fraud_Scams_%288528312890%29.jpg/1280px-%22Miracle_Cure%21%22_Health_Fraud_Scams_%288528312890%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/%22Miracle_Cure%21%22_Health_Fraud_Scams_%288528312890%29.jpg/500px-%22Miracle_Cure%21%22_Health_Fraud_Scams_%288528312890%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The subjective effects of placebos may be related to expectations, yet similar effects have been noted in open-label studies.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A%22Miracle_Cure!%22_Health_Fraud_Scams_(8528312890).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/James_Gillray%2C_%22Metallic_Tractors%22%2C_showing_Elisha_Perkins_Wellcome_M0010466.jpg/500px-James_Gillray%2C_%22Metallic_Tractors%22%2C_showing_Elisha_Perkins_Wellcome_M0010466.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/James_Gillray%2C_%22Metallic_Tractors%22%2C_showing_Elisha_Perkins_Wellcome_M0010466.jpg/1280px-James_Gillray%2C_%22Metallic_Tractors%22%2C_showing_Elisha_Perkins_Wellcome_M0010466.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/James_Gillray%2C_%22Metallic_Tractors%22%2C_showing_Elisha_Perkins_Wellcome_M0010466.jpg/500px-James_Gillray%2C_%22Metallic_Tractors%22%2C_showing_Elisha_Perkins_Wellcome_M0010466.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A quack treating a patient with Perkins Patent Tractors by James Gillray, 1801. John Haygarth used this remedy to illustrate the power of the placebo effect.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJames_Gillray%2C_%22Metallic_Tractors%22%2C_showing_Elisha_Perkins_Wellcome_M0010466.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/FestivalSudoeste2001.jpg/500px-FestivalSudoeste2001.jpg?utm